# Normalise text to LF in the repository, and check it out as LF.
#
# Why: the mobile CI job runs `npm run format:check` (Prettier), and Prettier's
# `endOfLine: lf` treats a CRLF file as unformatted - so a file committed from a
# Windows checkout fails the gate even though no content changed. That already
# cost one PR (#955, OrderCard.test.tsx). Nothing in .gitattributes stopped it,
# and any of the files renormalised below would do it again on the next edit.
* text=auto eol=lf

# The OTA signing certificate is verified byte-for-byte by
# mobile/scripts/check-update-signing.mjs, so its line endings are part of the
# file's identity. Never normalise it.
mobile/certs/certificate.pem -text

# Windows batch files need CRLF to execute; cmd.exe mis-parses LF-only scripts.
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.bat text eol=crlf